    Bug 544066 - Refactor nsMsgDatabase::MarkHdrRead and confine NNTP specific code to nsNewsDatabase. r=mkmelin


    For newsgroups, the read state of the individual messages is not only saved in
    the message headers contained in the database, it is also maintained in a key
    set, that is persisted in the db folder info as well as the newsrc file of the
    news server.

    The key set maintained in the newsrc file enables previous articles that have
    not yet been downloaded to be marked as read, ensuring that the 'Get Next …
    News Messages' function works as expected when the 'Mark remaining headers
    read' option was selected during header download.

    This patch simplifies the mechanism by having just MarkHdrRead() overridden by
    nsNewsDatabase to handle the maintainance of the key sets, while removing all
    the NNTP specific code from nsMsgDatabase and having IsHeaderRead working
    exactly the same for both kind of databases, thus ultimately fixing the actual
    bug.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D259403

